---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Meridian Owl Advisory"
  description="Learn about Meridian Owl Advisory and founder Lindsey Lamb's approach to governance, cybersecurity, privacy, and risk."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About Meridian Owl</p>

        <h1>
          Clear thinking for
          <span>complex systems.</span>
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p>
          Meridian Owl Advisory helps organizations make
          thoughtful, defensible decisions about governance,
          cybersecurity, privacy, and emerging technology.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div class="story-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The name</p>

        <h2>
          Direction, discernment,
          and a wider field of view.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p class="lead">
          Meridian Owl was built around two ideas:
          finding a reliable point of reference and seeing
          what others may overlook.
        </p>

        <p>
          A meridian is a line of orientation. It provides
          direction, establishes a shared reference point,
          and helps people understand where they are in
          relation to where they need to go.
        </p>

        <p>
          The owl represents discernment, curiosity, and
          the ability to navigate uncertain environments
          with clarity. Together, those ideas reflect the
          purpose of Meridian Owl Advisory: helping
          organizations understand complex risk and move
          forward with confidence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="founder-section">
    <div class="container founder-grid">
      <div class="founder-card">
        <img
          class="founder-photo"
          src="/images/Lindsey.png"
          alt="Lindsey Lamb, founder of Meridian Owl Advisory"
           width="800"
           height="1000"
         />

        <div class="founder-card-copy">
          <p class="founder-name">Lindsey Lamb</p>
          <p>Founder and Principal Advisor</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="founder-content">
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder</p>

        <h2>
          Translating complexity into
          practical decisions.
        </h2>

        <p class="lead">
          Lindsey Lamb brings a systems-oriented approach
          to governance, cybersecurity, privacy, compliance,
          and organizational risk.
        </p>

        <p>
          Her work focuses on helping leaders understand
          technical and regulatory issues without losing
          sight of business objectives, operational
          realities, or the people responsible for carrying
          the work forward.
        </p>

        <p>
          Lindsey has experience working across governance,
          risk, security, privacy, and compliance programs,
          including environments shaped by frameworks and
          requirements such as NIST, ISO 27001, SOC 2,
          HIPAA, and GDPR.
        </p>

        <p>
          She is especially interested in the intersection
          of cybersecurity, digital privacy, healthcare,
          artificial intelligence, and responsible
          technology governance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="perspective-section">
    <div class="container perspective-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A different perspective</p>

        <h2>
          Serious work does not require
          a generic point of view.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="perspective-copy">
        <p class="lead">
          Meridian Owl is intentionally thoughtful,
          curious, and a little unconventional.
        </p>

        <p>
          The firm draws inspiration from exploration,
          science fiction, games, technical communities,
          and the kinds of difficult questions that reward
          patience and systems thinking.
        </p>

        <p>
          That perspective supports a consulting style
          grounded in asking better questions, examining
          assumptions, and finding practical paths through
          ambiguity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">How the work is approached</p>

          <h2>
            Thoughtful guidance,
            grounded in reality.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          Effective advisory work should strengthen an
          organization’s judgment and capability—not create
          dependency.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principles-grid">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Context before prescription</h3>
          <p>
            Recommendations should reflect the organization,
            its mission, its constraints, and its actual
            risk environment.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Clarity over theater</h3>
          <p>
            Security and compliance work should produce
            useful decisions, not unnecessary complexity or
            performative documentation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Progress over perfection</h3>
          <p>
            Strong programs are built through prioritized,
            sustainable improvement—not impossible lists of
            ideal-state requirements.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Curiosity as a discipline</h3>
          <p>
            Good risk work begins by asking what is missing,
            what has been assumed, and what may change next.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container cta-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Work with Meridian Owl</p>

        <h2>
          Bring the complicated problem.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p>
          A first conversation can help clarify what is
          happening, what matters most, and what a useful
          engagement might look like.
        </p>

        <a class="button" href="/contact">
          Start a conversation
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-9);

    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 82% 35%,
        rgb(182 140 63 / 18%),
        transparent 28rem
      ),
      var(--color-cream-50);
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: end;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 55rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  h1 span {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-gold-600);
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .hero-copy p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .story-section,
  .principles-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-9);
    background: var(--color-white);
  }

  .story-grid,
  .perspective-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
    gap: var(--space-9);
  }

  .story-heading {
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .story-copy,
  .perspective-copy {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--color-navy-950);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.3vw, 1.65rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .founder-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-9);

    background: var(--color-cream-100);
  }

  .founder-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr;
    gap: var(--space-9);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .founder-card {
    overflow: hidden;

    border: var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-medium);

    background: var(--color-white);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }
  .founder-photo {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 22rem;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: center top;
}
@media (max-width: 54rem) {
  .founder-photo {
    height: 20rem;
  }
}

  .portrait-placeholder {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;

    min-height: 24rem;

    background:
      linear-gradient(
        rgb(8 26 47 / 12%),
        rgb(8 26 47 / 32%)
      ),
      radial-gradient(
        circle at center,
        var(--color-navy-700),
        var(--color-navy-950)
      );
  }

  .portrait-placeholder span {
    color: var(--color-gold-300);

    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .founder-card-copy {
    padding: var(--space-5);
  }

  .founder-card-copy p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .founder-name {
    color: var(--color-navy-950);

    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .founder-content {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .founder-content h2 {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .perspective-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-9);

    background: var(--color-navy-950);
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .perspective-section h2 {
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .perspective-section p {
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 72%);
  }

  .perspective-section .lead {
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: end;
  }

  .section-heading h2 {
    max-width: 45rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .section-heading > p {
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);

    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .principles-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-7);

    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .principles-grid article {
    padding-top: var(--space-5);

    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-gold-600);
  }

  .principles-grid article > span {
    color: var(--color-gold-600);

    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .principles-grid h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .cta-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);

    background: var(--color-gold-300);
  }

  .cta-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .cta-grid h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .cta-grid .eyebrow,
  .cta-grid p {
    color: var(--color-navy-950);
  }

  .cta-grid .button {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 54rem) {
    .hero-grid,
    .story-grid,
    .founder-grid,
    .perspective-grid,
    .section-heading,
    .cta-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .principles-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .founder-card {
      max-width: 31rem;
    }

    .portrait-placeholder {
      min-height: 20rem;
    }
  }
</style>